<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Westinghouse.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Westinghouse.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Morgan Stanley analyst Frank Bodencheck said he started co-coverage of Westinghouse Electric Corp with analyst Jennifer Pokrzywinski ahead of the breakup of Westinghouse into separate media and industrial businesses.</p>
<p>-- Bodencheck cited a recent decline in Westinghouse share price for outperform rating.</p>
<p>-- Forecasts pro forma 1997 EBITDA at $1.2 billion, which includes cash flow from TNN and CMT acquisitions.</p>
<p>-- Set $20-22 per share target for 1997 and $25 target for 1998.</p>
<p>-- Shares rose one to 18-3/8 in early activity.</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street desk, 212-859-1730))</p>
</text>
